PART A  Deser-Levin / T - T_Lambda family
  [OK] A0  (5D embedding, Milgrom eq 7) a^2 + H^2 = H^2/f for the static dS observer, i.e. T_DL = T_dS/sqrt(f) (Tolman)  -- exact
  [OK] A1  2 pi (T - T_Lambda) = a * muhat(a / (2H))  with a0hat = 2H  (Milgrom 1999 eq 8-9)
  [OK] A2  small-a limit: 2 pi Delta T = a^2/(2H) + O(a^4)   =>  F = a^2/(2H)
  [OK] A3  setting F = m a_N gives a^2 = a_N * (2H): deep-MOND with a0 = 2H  (this is the coefficient: Z = H/a0 = 1/2)
  [OK] A4  Klinkhamer-Kopp A0 = 4 pi T_min with 2 pi T_min = H  =>  A0 = 2H  (their eq 9)
  [OK] A5  Pikhitsa mu(x)=sqrt(1+1/x^2)-1/x with x=g/H equals muhat(g/(2H)): the same function, a0 = 2H
  [OK] A6  Smolin F/m = sqrt(a^2+H^2) - H = a*muhat(a/2H): the same function
  [OK] A7  Milgrom's other functional a dT/da gives a*x/sqrt(1+x^2) with x = a/H, small-a a^2/H: a0 = H  (coefficient depends on the inserted functional: 2 vs 1)
  [OK] A8  CONTROL: T^2 - T_Lambda^2 = a^2/(4 pi^2) has no H in it, so it defines no acceleration scale (d/dH = 0)
  [OK] A9  CONTROL: without the subtraction, 2 pi T(a=0) = H != 0: a freely falling detector would feel a force (Smolin's reason for the subtraction)
  [OK] A10 a0(T-T_Lambda) / a0(framework) = 2 Z_fw = 2 sqrt(32 pi/3) = 11.5776  (the route lands ~11.6x ABOVE the framework value)
  [OK] A11 a0(T-T_Lambda) / a0(Milgrom empirical cH/2pi) = 4 pi exactly (12.57): the derived coefficient misses the empirical one by a solid angle

PART B  Ho-Minic-Ng: the coefficient is the inserted 1/pi
  [OK] B1  small-a: F/m = a^2/(2 a_Lambda)  (their eq after (4))
  [OK] B2  a_MOND^2 = a_N * (beta a_Lambda / 2), i.e. a_c = beta a_Lambda / 2
  [OK] B3  with their beta = 1/pi:  a_c = a_Lambda/(2 pi)  (their 'set a_c = a0/(2 pi) for simplicity'): the 1/pi IS the coefficient, put in by hand
  [OK] B4  MUTATION beta = 1 gives a_c = a_Lambda/2 (a factor pi larger): the coefficient moves one-for-one with the inserted beta
  [OK] B5  CONTROL beta = 0 (no M'): a^2/(2 a_Lambda) = a_N, i.e. NO MOND (Newton again), as they state; the DL entropic force alone does not give MOND

